ITEMS=[]
def Q(stem,key,d1,d2,d3,why):ITEMS.append((stem,[key,d1,d2,d3],why))
Q('Which aid tells the operator the boom\'s inclination rather than the load\'s weight?',
 'A boom-angle indicator','A load-moment indicator','A boom-length indicator','A drum-rotation indicator',
 'A boom-angle indicator shows boom inclination. A load-moment indicator works from load and radius, and a length indicator shows extension, not angle.')
Q('Which aid prevents or warns of the hook assembly being drawn up into the boom tip?',
 'An anti-two-block device','A load-moment limiter','A boom-hoist limiting device','A drum-rotation indicator',
 'An anti-two-block device addresses contact between the lower block or ball and the boom tip or upper block. A boom-hoist limiter stops the boom being raised too far, a different hazard.')
Q('Which aid helps an operator detect motion of a hoist drum that cannot be seen directly?',
 'A drum-rotation indicator','A drum brake lock','A hoist line-pull meter','A boom-angle indicator',
 'A drum-rotation indicator reports drum movement to the operator. A line-pull meter shows force, not whether the drum is turning.')
Q('Which aid directly indicates the weight being supported rather than boom geometry or drum movement?',
 'A load-weighing device','A boom-angle indicator','A drum-rotation indicator','A boom-length indicator',
 'A load-weighing device indicates load weight, subject to its proper setup and limitations. The other aids report geometry or drum motion.')
Q('Which safety device provides the operator with information needed to check whether the machine sits true on its supports?',
 'A crane-level indicator','A boom-angle indicator','An outrigger position sensor','A load-moment indicator',
 'OSHA 1926.1415 requires a crane-level indicator on covered equipment, with specified exceptions. An outrigger sensor reports extension, not whether the machine is level.')
Q('Which safety device provides an immediately available audible warning to people around the crane?',
 'A horn within the operator\'s reach','A rotating beacon on the cab','A radio to the signal person','An anti-two-block alarm',
 'A horn must be built in or immediately available to the operator under 1926.1415. A beacon is visual, and a radio reaches only the signal person.')
Q('Which required hydraulic-outrigger feature helps retain the jack\'s support against unintended hydraulic movement?',
 'An integral holding valve','A manual pin through the beam','An outrigger position sensor','A pressure gauge on each jack',
 'Hydraulic outrigger and stabilizer jacks require an integral holding device or check valve. A gauge only shows pressure; it does not hold it.')
Q('Which required device keeps an equipped foot-pedal brake in its selected holding position?',
 'A lock on the brake pedal','A pedal return spring','A pedal-brake warning light','A parking brake on the carrier',
 'Equipment with foot-pedal brakes must have locks under 1926.1415. A return spring does the opposite of holding the pedal down.')
Q('A blind lift depends on radio signals, and the radio link suddenly fails. What is the required response?',
 'Stop until communication is restored','Finish the lift using hand signals','Continue slowly with the horn','Let the operator judge the landing',
 'Operations requiring signals must be safely stopped until communication is reestablished and a proper signal is understood. In a blind lift, hand signals cannot be seen.')
Q('A special attachment cannot be directed with the standard hand-signal method. What must the operator, signal person and lift director do before using non-standard hand signals?',
 'Agree on them before the operation','Write them on the load itself','Use the standard set anyway','Let the signal person improvise',
 'Non-standard signals must be agreed before the operation under 1926.1419(c)(2). Improvised signals risk being misread.')
Q('A signal person faces the operator from the opposite side of the load. From whose viewpoint must left/right directions be expressed?',
 'The operator\'s','The signal person\'s','The load\'s direction of travel','The lift director\'s',
 'All directions must use the operator\'s perspective, which avoids reversed instructions when the signal person faces the cab.')
Q('One signal person communicates with two cranes on a coordination channel. What must make each instruction\'s intended recipient clear?',
 'Naming the crane before each command','A louder voice for the nearer crane','Giving both cranes the same instruction','Hand signals in place of radio',
 'The crane must be identified before the function and direction, or by an equally effective method, so neither operator acts on the other\'s instruction.')
Q('Before a radio-controlled lift begins, what checks that signal transmission is clear, effective and reliable at that site?',
 'An on-site test of the devices','The radio supplier\'s certificate','A test done at the yard last week','The signal person\'s experience',
 'The transmitting devices must be tested on site before operations under 1926.1420(a); local interference cannot be checked anywhere else.')
Q('Which reception arrangement lets the operator hear transmitted instructions without holding a communication device?',
 'A hands-free receiver','A handheld radio on the console','A phone held to one ear','A speaker mounted outside the cab',
 'OSHA 1926.1420(c) requires hands-free reception by the operator. A speaker outside the cab may not be heard over engine noise.')
Q('Ordinary unrelated radio traffic is interfering with lift instructions. Which channel arrangement does OSHA generally require, subject to its stated coordination exceptions?',
 'A dedicated signal channel','A shared site channel','Any open channel nearby','A cell phone line',
 'Signal transmission generally uses a dedicated channel, with specified exceptions for coordinated operations. A shared channel is what lets the unrelated traffic in.')
Q('The operator and signal person use different spoken languages. What must be established for voice signals to be effective?',
 'A language all parties understand','A translator at the cab door','Hand signals only, with no voice','Signals spoken more loudly',
 'The operator, signal person and lift director must be able to communicate effectively in the language used.')
Q('Before two cranes support one load, who must develop the lift plan?',
 'A qualified person','Either crane operator','The site safety officer','The rigger on the ground',
 'A qualified person develops the multiple-crane lift plan under 1926.1432(a). An operator may help but is not named for it by role.')
Q('Who must review a multiple-crane lift plan in a meeting with all workers involved before implementing the lift?',
 'The lift director','The plan\'s author only','The crane owner','Each crane operator',
 'The lift director reviews the plan with the involved workers under 1926.1432(b).')
Q('For a power-line plan using Table A, who provides the requested line-voltage information?',
 'The utility owner or operator','The crane operator','The local building inspector','The site electrician',
 'The utility owner/operator provides voltage information under 1926.1408(c).')
Q('A worker other than the designated signal person sees someone enter immediate danger. Who may give the emergency-stop signal?',
 'Anyone who sees the danger','Only the designated signal person','Only the lift director','Only the A/D director',
 'Anyone aware of a safety problem may give the stop or emergency-stop signal, and the operator must obey it.')
Q('Under OSHA 1926.1417(o)(3)(ii), an operator begins hoisting and the load moment indicator shows the load exceeds 75% of maximum rated capacity at the longest radius to be used. What must happen next?',
 'Confirm it by source or calculation','Proceed, since the indicator has weighed it','Reduce speed and proceed','Add counterweight and proceed',
 'Under 1926.1417(o)(3)(ii) the operator must not proceed until the weight is verified under (o)(3)(i): an industry-recognised source, a recognised calculation method or other equally reliable means. The indicator reading alone does not clear the lift, and extra counterweight beyond the specification is never allowed.')
Q('A competent person identifies slack rope that requires re-spooling. What must be verified as slack is removed before lifting?',
 'Correct seating on drum and sheaves','The rope is fully unwound','The hook is resting on the ground mat','The boom is at minimum angle',
 'Under 1926.1417(m) the rope must be properly seated on the drum and in the sheaves as slack is removed.')
Q('Immediately before starting the engine, what operational check does OSHA require?',
 'Controls set and personnel clear','Fuel level and oil checked','Load chart reviewed with the rigger first','Horn tested twice',
 'The operator verifies that controls are in their proper starting positions and that all personnel are clear.')
Q('The setup requires ballast, and spare ballast is available nearby. What must determine the amount installed?',
 'The manufacturer\'s specified amount','All the spare that is available','The heaviest the carrier can hold','The operator\'s estimate of the load',
 'The manufacturer-specified counterweight or ballast must be installed, and the specified maximum must not be exceeded. Adding spare weight can overload the machine.')
Q('A required horn stops working, and no other compliant horn is immediately available. What must happen before crane operation resumes?',
 'The horn must be repaired first','Use hand signals in its place','Run for up to 7 days meanwhile','Run for up to 30 days meanwhile',
 'A horn is a required safety device; 1926.1415 does not permit alternative measures. The 7 and 30 day periods apply to operational aids, not safety devices.')
Q('A listed operational aid fails, and OSHA\'s provision for that aid names a stopgap method for the repair period. Any stricter manufacturer measures are also met. What allows operation to continue after a safe stop?',
 'Using the alternative measure OSHA lists','No operation until the aid is fixed','A higher rated capacity','Doubling the number of signal persons',
 'For an operational aid, the temporary alternative named in 1926.1416 may be used during the allowed repair period. Stopping until repair is the rule for safety devices.')
Q('The only load chart in the cab is electronic, and its display fails. Which condition must be restored after safely stopping?',
 'Access to the rated capacities','Power to the cab heater','The radio link to the ground','A paper inspection log',
 'Rated capacities must again be accessible to the operator, electronically or otherwise, before operations resume.')
Q('An operator determines that equipment adjustments or repairs are necessary. What communication is required to the employer\'s designated recipient and next operator on successive shifts?',
 'Prompt written notice','A spoken mention at shift end','A call after the job finishes','A note in next month\'s log',
 'Under 1926.1417(j) the operator must promptly inform those persons in writing.')
Q('A tag line is needed within a power-line encroachment-control plan. What type is required?',
 'A nonconductive tag line','A wire-rope tag line','A damp natural-fibre line','A steel-cored synthetic line',
 'Tag lines used under 1926.1408(b) must be nonconductive. A wet natural-fibre or metal-cored line can conduct.')
Q('A supplier\'s equipment package has no marked weight. Which information is needed to establish the load\'s mass before lifting by a reliable-source method?',
 'A shipping or maker\'s weight record','The rigger\'s estimate by eye','The chart capacity at that radius','Its marked dimensions only',
 'A manufacturer record or other equally reliable weight information supports capacity verification. Chart capacity is the limit, not the load.')
Q('A crew proposes moving the crane with a suspended load. Which equipment-specific instruction must be checked for a prohibition on that practice?',
 'The manufacturer\'s procedures','The site traffic plan','The rigging manufacturer\'s catalogue','The general OSHA travel table',
 'Travel with a load is prohibited if the manufacturer prohibits it; other supervised-travel requirements also apply.')
Q('A suspended load starts swinging outward as the upperworks rotate. Which operating variable must be limited to keep the load within a controllable radius?',
 'Swing speed','Hoist speed','Boom length','Travel speed',
 'Rotational speed must keep the load from swinging out beyond a radius at which it can be controlled.')
Q('A competent person reassesses equipment stability and rated capacity as weather worsens. Which conditions is OSHA 1926.1417(n) specifically addressing?',
 'Wind, ice and snow','Heat, humidity and dust','Darkness and glare','Fog and light drizzle',
 'Wind, ice and snow can affect stability and rated capacity and require appropriate adjustment under 1926.1417(n).')
Q('A wheeled crane is permitted to travel with a load. Which wheel-related condition must meet manufacturer specifications?',
 'Tire inflation pressure','Wheel nut paint marks','Tire tread pattern','Rim width',
 'The specified tire pressure must be maintained when traveling with a load.')
Q('The intended swing path brings the boom beside a building projection. Which condition must remain satisfied throughout movement?',
 'No part of the equipment touches it','The boom stays within 2 feet of it','The swing alarm keeps sounding','The load stays below half capacity',
 'The boom and other parts of the equipment must not contact obstructions under 1926.1417(p).')
Q('A long suspended assembly can turn and strike workers. What condition makes a tag or restraint line necessary under the operating rule?',
 'Hazardous rotation of the load','Any lift over a set weight','Any load longer than the boom','Every lift on the site',
 'A tag or restraint line is required when necessary to prevent hazardous rotation of the load.')
Q('A valid emergency-stop signal is given during hoisting. What is the operator\'s response?',
 'Bring the motion to a safe stop','Finish the hoist, then stop','Find out who gave it, then stop','Lower the load quickly',
 'A stop or emergency-stop signal must be obeyed whoever gives it; the operator safely stops the operation.')
Q('The planned movement remains within the verified capacity and clearances, communication is reliable, no safety problem exists, and the designated signal person gives the agreed hoist signal. What is appropriate?',
 'Hoist as signalled, under control','Wait for a second signal person','Stop and request a new lift plan','Stop and recheck the radio',
 'With all stated conditions met, the operator makes the authorised controlled movement; nothing in the scenario calls for a stop.')
Q('A load\'s destination is moved farther from the crane than the plan allowed for. What must happen before the load is moved there?',
 'Check the new radius against the chart','Proceed slowly while watching the load','Raise the boom to keep the hook high','Add a tag line and continue',
 'A greater radius can lower the rated capacity, so the new radius and configuration must be checked against the chart before the move.')
Q('The load has been landed and the shift is ending. What must the operator do before leaving the crane unattended?',
 'Complete the specified shutdown steps','Leave the engine idling','Hang the block at full height','Leave the key for the next crew',
 'Follow the manufacturer\'s shutdown and securing procedures; landing the load does not complete shutdown.')
Q('For a stated reeving plan, four supporting parts are each allowed 2,000 lb and the plan ignores efficiency losses. What is the line-limited load, before checking other crane limits?',
 '8,000 pounds','2,000 pounds','6,000 pounds','10,000 pounds',
 '4 x 2,000 = 8,000 lb. Actual reeving information and all crane limits still govern.')
Q('An operator will handle a load at 90% of a stated 10,000 lb maximum line pull. What line force marks that 90% threshold?',
 '9,000 pounds','7,500 pounds','10,000 pounds','1,000 pounds',
 '0.90 x 10,000 = 9,000 lb; the OSHA brake-test threshold refers to maximum line pull, not chart capacity.')
Q('A documented load consists of an 8,500 lb component plus 1,500 lb of included contents. What total load weight must be considered before adding separate lifting gear?',
 '10,000 pounds','8,500 pounds','7,000 pounds','11,500 pounds',
 '8,500 + 1,500 = 10,000 lb; contents are part of the load. Gear deductions or additions still follow the chart notes.')
Q('A verified 16,000 lb maximum rated capacity applies at the longest radius. What is 75% of that capacity for the OSHA load-weight verification threshold?',
 '12,000 pounds','4,000 pounds','16,000 pounds','10,000 pounds',
 '0.75 x 16,000 = 12,000 lb; 4,000 lb is the remaining 25%. Exceeding 12,000 lb under the indicating-device method requires reliable weight verification.')
Q('A required boom-angle/radius indicator fails during repair. What specified temporary method determines the geometry?',
 'Measure the radius or angle with a device','Estimate the radius and angle by eye','Use the last reading recorded','Read the boom-length marks',
 'Under 1926.1416(e)(1) the radius or boom angle is measured with a measuring device; an estimate by eye is not a measurement.')
Q('A telescopic boom-length indicator fails. Which listed temporary method directly establishes boom length?',
 'Marked or measured length of the boom','Use the boom length from the last lift','Estimate it from the boom angle','Count the hydraulic pump strokes',
 'Measured marks on the boom or direct measurement are among the permitted alternatives under 1926.1416(e)(3).')
Q('An outrigger-extension monitor fails during repair. What must the operator verify before operations requiring outrigger deployment?',
 'The actual outrigger positions','The monitor\'s fuse rating','The outrigger hydraulic pressure','The tire pressure',
 'The actual outrigger or stabilizer position must be verified as correct under the manufacturer\'s procedures. Pressure does not show extension.')
Q('An out-of-view hoist drum\'s rotation indicator fails. What listed temporary measure allows drum movement to be observed?',
 'A drum mark visible by mirror or camera','Listening for drum noise','Counting turns of the hoist lever','A second operator watching the hook block',
 'Under 1926.1416(e)(5) the drum is marked and mirrors or video are provided if necessary so the operator can see the mark.')
Q('Repetitive duty-cycle lifts each exceed 90% of maximum line pull. When does the OSHA few-inches lift-and-brake test apply within that repetitive sequence?',
 'On the first lift only','On every lift in the sequence','On every tenth lift','Only after the brake slips',
 'For duty-cycle or repetitive lifts at that threshold, the test applies to the first lift, not every successive lift.')
Q('During assembly, the crew plans to rely on the boom-hoist brake to prevent movement. When must that brake\'s ability to hold be tested?',
 'Before any reliance is placed on it','After assembly is complete','At the next annual inspection','Only if it has slipped before',
 'Under 1926.1404(h)(10) the brake must be tested to determine that it holds before reliance is placed on it.')
Q('The operator has stopped after discovering a safety problem that must be discussed with the signal person. When may the operation resume?',
 'When both agree it is resolved','When the lift director arrives','After a set ten-minute pause','When the operator alone decides',
 'Both the operator and signal person must agree that the problem has been resolved before operations resume under 1926.1419(g).')
Q('A crew proposes using a different set of voice commands halfway through a job. When must the operator, signal person and lift director agree on the revised commands?',
 'Before the new commands are used','At the end of the job','At the next morning meeting','Only if a near miss occurs',
 'They must agree before using changed voice signals; the earlier agreement does not cover the change.')
Q('A loaded boom bends downward and its tip moves farther horizontally from the axis of rotation. Which chart-related change must be considered?',
 'A longer working radius','A higher boom angle','A shorter boom length','A lighter hook block',
 'The load radius increases; capacity must be assessed at the actual loaded geometry.')
Q('A submerged object is lifted until it emerges from the water. Which change can increase the force carried by the crane?',
 'Reduced buoyancy','Cooler hoist rope','Lower wind at the surface','Shorter hoist line',
 'Buoyant support decreases as the object leaves the water, so the crane carries more of its weight.')
Q('A moving suspended load is arrested abruptly instead of smoothly. Which effect can increase forces beyond the static load?',
 'A dynamic shock load','A lighter static load','Reduced line tension','Increased buoyancy',
 'Abrupt acceleration or stopping introduces dynamic force, commonly called shock loading.')
Q('A crew tries to drag a load sideways with the hoist line instead of lifting vertically. Which force is imposed on the boom?',
 'A side load on the boom','Extra vertical load only','A pure compression load','Less load than a straight lift',
 'Side pulling imposes lateral loading the boom is not rated for; OSHA 1926.1417(q) prohibits dragging or pulling loads sideways.')
assert len(ITEMS)==56
